title: Max's plugin dev norms mean code is often moved from /src/ to / within the plugin directory. so the info.toml entries need to be without 'src/'. We should support extra search dirs for export files (keeping their path if the have one). so we check <export_path> and if that's not found, we check <search_dir>/<export_path> too. This goes for normal and shared exports. This should make it work with most of Max's plugins.
updated_at: "2026-08-31T15:27:38Z"
---

Max's plugin dev norms mean code is often moved from /src/ to / within the plugin directory. so the info.toml entries need to be without 'src/'. We should support extra search dirs for export files (keeping their path if the have one). so we check <export_path> and if that's not found, we check <search_dir>/<export_path> too. This goes for normal and shared exports. This should make it work with most of Max's plugins.
